    "created_at": "2021-11-23T10:59:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-23T10:59:46Z",
    "body": "You're right, it's no longer sufficient to only ignore `AbortError` DOMExceptions. Following the suggestion in https://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/1027#pullrequestreview-782289936, we would need something along the lines of:\r\n```javascript\r\nAbortSignal.prototype.ignoreAborts = function (promise) {\r\n  promise = Promise.resolve(promise);\r\n\r\n  return promise.catch(e => {\r\n    if (this.aborted && e === this.reason) {\r\n      // swallow exception\r\n    } else {\r\n      // rethrow\r\n      throw e;\r\n    }\r\n  });\r\n};\r\n```\r\nwhich authors could use as:\r\n```javascript\r\nasync function butterBiscuits({ signal }) {\r\n  try {\r\n    const result = await signal.ignoreAborts(fetch('https://butternet/the-good-stuff?lots', { signal }));\r\n    if (result) {\r\n      this.biscuits.butter = result;\r\n    }\r\n  } catch (err) {\r\n    alerts.push('a TERRIBLE thing happened');\r\n    throw err;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\nIt's kind of weird that you have to use `signal` twice, though. 😕",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
