    "created_at": "2021-11-23T11:31:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-23T11:31:52Z",
    "body": "> It's kind of weird that you have to use `signal` twice, though. 😕\r\n\r\nI think in most cases you would only bother with it at the same level you create the `AbortSignal`, i.e. if you're just using a delegated signal you didn't create you'd usually just want to delegate error handling to the caller (as they raised the error).",
