    "created_at": "2021-11-23T12:41:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-23T12:41:26Z",
    "body": "@MattiasBuelens thanks, though it seems such an approach would still place special value on aborting. Also, `e === this.reason` would only work if there was no cloning involved.\r\n\r\nPerhaps @yuki3's https://github.com/whatwg/webidl/issues/933#issuecomment-718896274 is more applicable now, especially if we also introduce `AbortSignal.timeout()` (which would result in a \"`TimeoutError`\" `DOMException`). In essence it seems you want the ability to filter out certain exceptions. The tricky aspect to something like that would be bridging JS exceptions and `DOMException` somehow. Or perhaps each can have its own API and they can work together through chaining.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
