    "created_at": "2021-11-23T16:02:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-23T16:02:21Z",
    "body": "I still think `DOMException.ignoreAborts()`, which only ignores `\"AbortError\"` `DOMException`s, is a good idea. As I've stated over in https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/1033#issuecomment-974869224, I don't think the fact that you can change the reason, changes how consumers should treat the result. Most cases don't want a general \"ignore any abort reason\"; they want \"ignore `\"AbortError\"` `DOMException`\".\r\n\r\nIn particular, given the motivating case for branching out, i.e. `\"TimeoutError\"` `DOMException`, you generally *don't* want to ignore timeouts for a fetch. You want to tell the user: \"the operation timed out\". Whereas you *do* want to ignore aborts: the user is probably the one that caused an abort.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/webidl/issues/comments/976768023/reactions",
